# Quality and Deterministic CI Contract

## Definition of deterministic green
List the exact commands/jobs required for a merge candidate. Keep the list project-specific; do not add tools merely because OneCompany mentions them.

```text
format/check:
lint/static analysis:
typecheck/compile:
unit tests:
integration tests:
migration/compatibility tests:
smoke/browser/journey tests:
build/package:
security/dependency audit:
UI/accessibility/visual checks when applicable:
performance/budget checks when applicable:
```

## Reproducibility controls
Document what must be fixed or deliberately varied:
- runtime/tool versions and lockfiles;
- locale/timezone/clock;
- random seed;
- test data/fixtures;
- browser/device/runtime image;
- external network/provider mocks or test environments;
- fonts/assets for visual tests.

A test should fail for a meaningful behavior change, not because the clock, locale, random generator or public network happened to differ.

## Test strategy
- Unit:
- Integration:
- End-to-end/user journey:
- Contract/API/schema:
- Concurrency/property/adversarial:
- Migration/restart/replay:
- Security/privacy:
- Accessibility/visual/performance when user-facing:

## Test isolation
Tests must not depend on execution order unless that order is itself the contract. Clean up durable external fixtures. Parallel execution must not create cross-test data races.

## Retry policy
Retries are bounded and reserved for explicitly classified transient infrastructure failures. Product assertions are not retried until green.

## Flaky-test policy
A flaky required test is a defect to fix or explicitly quarantine through reviewed policy. Quarantine must remain visible and time-bounded; it is not permission to silently ignore red CI.

## Regression policy
Material BLOCKER/MAJOR defects should become durable regressions when technically meaningful. Prefer the smallest test that proves the original failure and its boundary conditions.

## Coverage policy
Coverage is diagnostic evidence, not the definition of quality. High coverage does not substitute for assertions on contracts, failure paths, concurrency, authorization, recovery or user journeys.

## Dependency and supply-chain policy
- use lockfiles/reproducible resolution where the ecosystem supports them;
- pin behavior-bearing CI actions/tools according to governance policy;
- review new runtime dependencies for necessity, license, maintenance, security and cost;
- do not make a hidden network download part of deterministic green without an explicit cache/provenance strategy.

## Performance policy
Define measurable budgets only where stable and useful. A noisy benchmark should inform review rather than create retry-until-green behavior.

## Exact-head rule
All required checks for merge correspond to the same candidate SHA that receives the independent final gate.
